      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm stuck on my lit review. if i have a source with 5 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for APA 7th edition? also how is that different from how i'd do it in chicago style? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a source with five authors in APA 7th edition, you'll use the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" from the very first citation onward.  In the text, it looks like this: (Smith et al., 2022).  The difference is that in Chicago style, you typically list all authors the first time, depending on the specific note or bibliography format you are using, but for parenthetical citations, it often involves listing the first author followed by \"et al.\" after the first few, though the rules can be more nuanced depending on whether you are using notes or author-date.",
